as so important to help educate kind of like the public and the education sector on is like this differentiation between what a tool is marketed as versus what we actually have the evidence, you know, to support its intended outcomes. Well, a lot of the debate right now around kids in tech has centered around screen time. But one of the reports' recommendations is to move beyond just screen time and talk instead about what screens are replacing. So why is it important to do this to move beyond screen time and what should we be thinking about instead? I'm so glad that you asked this question because I feel anybody turning on the news right now, you can't get through a half hour of it without hearing about kind of this screen time debate. And let me just say,

12
