say, I'm a mom. You know, I have two middle school kids. I completely understand why people start with screen time. It's, you can see it easily. It's easy to count. And I will say that screen time, it might be an appropriate metric for recreational uses of technology like Snapchat or a video game. But when we're talking about technology for learning, then screen time by itself, it tells us very little about whether a child is learning or whether that experience is helping the child to learn. So just let's take an example to play with. You know, if I tell you that a child spends 20 minutes on a screen, how much do you really know about that experience? The child could have been working very deeply through a math problem or like in Hudson's case, spend 20 minutes dressing a

