and we really have very little evidence that learning has occurred. So if it was me, and I promise you, I'm not only talking from, you know, executive lead psychologist had, I'm really thinking about what would be important to me as a mom. I would start to ask myself two questions when, you know, looking at my child kind of engaging in ed tech. I would ask, you know, does the feedback that they're getting through this app prompt my child to think more deeply than simply pointing them towards the right answer? And then if I had some evidence that that was the case, I would ask if there is credible evidence that the tool works for, you know, especially if I'm thinking from an educator's point of view or from the point of view of a teacher, that that tool works for students similar to those who will actually use it.

