I mean, do they have to design new tests? How will testing need to change in the face of new technology? This isn't really as difficult to uncover as we might think. I really, I would urge any parent out there to just look over the shoulder of what your child is doing for no more than two minutes. And I think you will be able to tell whether that app is really resulting in learning or not. But the true test is going to be not what happens when the child is using the app. It's what happens next. So shut down the community. computer, close the laptop, and ask the child, the student to remember the idea, to explain it in their own words or to use that knowledge in a new situation once those prompts are gone. Do you remember those keyboards, Kim, that used to, I think they still have them. They used to light up, like the keys would light up to tell you, like, what button to press. This was marketed for years as a way to teach folks how to play piano. It's a little like,

