that, you may play the piano perfectly when those lights are lighting up for you and telling you which buttons to press, but we find out what you actually learned when those lights go away. And that's the same thing that we're going to do now. It's not going to be so much about like evaluating what's happening in the learning experience itself. It's going to be evaluating what happens after that learning experience and then using that information to kind of then make judgments about how effective that educational experience was. Are there certain types of learning or even academic topics that ed tech is particularly well suited for and others that it's not?

